## Run

```bash
composer install
cp .env.example .env
php artisan key:generate           # populate APP_KEY
touch database/database.sqlite     # create the SQLite file
php artisan migrate                # apply the generated migrations
php artisan serve                  # start on http://localhost:8000
```

All API routes are registered in `routes/api.php`, which Laravel serves under the **`/api`**
prefix — e.g. `GET /api/<%= view.entities[0] ? view.entities[0].table : "items" %>`.

## The generated boundary

Everything under **`app/Generated/`** (PSR-4 `App\Generated\…`) and every file in
`database/migrations/` is **owned by Backbone**: it is regenerated wholesale on the next run, so
never hand-edit it. Everything else — `public/index.php`, `bootstrap/`, `config/`,
`routes/console.php` — is written **once** and is yours to extend.

```
app/Generated/
  Models/              # Eloquent models ($fillable, $casts, relations)
  Http/Controllers/    # API resource controllers (JSON responses)
  Http/Requests/       # Store/Update form requests (validation rules)
<% if (auth) { %>  Models/User.php + Http/Controllers/AuthController.php  # register / login / me
<% } %>database/migrations/  # one Schema::create class per table (owned)
routes/api.php         # apiResource + auth routes (owned — matches the Blueprint)
```

`routes/api.php` is owned too, so regenerating keeps it in sync with your entities. To add custom
routes, create your own route file and include it from `bootstrap/app.php`.

## API shape

The JSON API is **snake_case** — the native Eloquent attribute casing — so request bodies and
responses use column names directly (e.g. `<%= view.entities[0] && view.entities[0].writable[0] ? view.entities[0].writable[0].name : "title" %>`).

